    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is just another one of <i>those</i> games \u2014 the kind designed to stir up that dormant frustration inside you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a colored square trying to climb your way up a minimalistic, color-coded gauntlet. The rule is simple: <strong>you can only touch objects that match your current color</strong>. Mess that up, and you'll fall. And not just a little \u2014 you'll plummet <i>all the way down</i> through every layer you\u2019ve already passed.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple controls. Brutal consequences. Unfair design that somehow always feels fair \u2014 until it doesn\u2019t.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you\u2019re the kind of player who laughs in the face of pain, this one\u2019s for you.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is just another one of <i>those</i> games \u2014 the kind designed to stir up that dormant frustration inside you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a colored square trying to climb your way up a minimalistic, color-coded gauntlet. The rule is simple: <strong>you can only touch objects that match your current color</strong>. Mess that up, and you'll fall. And not just a little \u2014 you'll plummet <i>all the way down</i> through every layer you\u2019ve already passed.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple controls. Brutal consequences. Unfair design that somehow always feels fair \u2014 until it doesn\u2019t.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you\u2019re the kind of player who laughs in the face of pain, this one\u2019s for you.</p>",
    "short_description": "A brutally minimal precision platformer where you play as a shifting-colored square, only able to touch objects that match your color \u2014 fall once, and drop through every layer you've already climbed.",
